ascii2web
=========

Two programs to change ascii into unicode for use on the web.
One changes CP-437 ascii to unicode `&#xxxx;` entities, and the other UTF-8 code
(which isn't always needed as the web works with UTF-8, but it was a fun bit of
code to write).

The project also includes a browser-only JavaScript converter in `index.html`.
It can convert uploaded or pasted CP-437/UTF-8 text into HTML numeric entities
and renders the preview safely with `textContent` so pasted markup is displayed
as text instead of being executed as HTML.

Run locally
-----------

From this directory, start a local static server:

```sh
python3 -m http.server 8000
```

Then open <http://localhost:8000/> for the JavaScript converter.

Safety notes
------------

The JavaScript converter keeps two separate outputs:

* **HTML entity output**: the generated `&#xxxx;` string you can copy.
* **Safe preview**: decoded text assigned through `textContent`, not raw
  `innerHTML`, so input such as `<script>` is shown as text.

Thanks to Adriel for the challenge.
